### Keep the unavailable eraser shortcut from clearing LiveDraw

**Severity:** `high`

LiveDraw intentionally does not support the scrub eraser, but the current `Shift+E` branch only handles the non-layered case. In a layered LiveDraw window it falls through to the existing plain-`E` path and clears every annotation. Consume `Shift+E` before that fallback so the unavailable shortcut is a no-op instead of a destructive clear. A regression around the production `case 'E'` dispatch confirms this preserves plain-`E` clearing, the non-layered eraser cycle, and typing-mode behavior.

```suggestion
            if( ( GetKeyState( VK_SHIFT ) & 0x8000 ) &&
                ( GetWindowLong( hWnd, GWL_EXSTYLE ) & WS_EX_LAYERED ) != 0 ) {
                break;
            }

            // Shift+E cycles the scrub eraser tool: off -> pixel -> stroke -> off.
```
